  m_Name: Shaft
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Shaft
  description: The Shaft is a crucial component located at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, made of Shaft1 material, and has a small, thin-flat shape.
    It plays a vital role in connecting and transmitting power between the turbine
    and compressor sections, enabling the engine to generate thrust. Interestingly,
    the Shaft's thin-flat design allows for minimal weight while maintaining exceptional
    strength and durability.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d11fc28afc9aa33439fa837310607453, type: 3}
